 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nNamespace package detection broken for setuptools packages\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen trying to import modules from setuptools namespace packages, astroid incorrectly identifies them as namespace packages when they shouldn't be, or fails to identify them when they should be. This affects module resolution and can cause import errors.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport astroid\n\n# Try to get AST from a setuptools namespace package\nmgr = astroid.AstroidManager()\ntry:\n    module = mgr.ast_from_module_name('some_namespace_package')\n    print(\"Successfully imported:\", module)\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\"Failed to import:\", e)\n```\n\nThe issue also affects zip-based package imports where the namespace detection logic incorrectly processes the package structure.\n\n#### Expected vs Actual Behavior\n\nExpected: Setuptools namespace packages should be correctly identified based on their `__init__.py` content containing `pkg_resources` and `declare_namespace(__name__)` calls, or pkgutil-style packages with `extend_path` calls.\n\nActual: The namespace detection logic returns incorrect results, causing import failures for legitimate namespace packages or incorrectly treating regular packages as namespace packages.\n</issue>\n",
